{"seed":{"mim":"600501","entry_type":"phenotype","prefix":"#","title":"ABCD SYNDROME","alt_titles":["ALBINISM, BLACK LOCK, CELL MIGRATION DISORDER OF THE NEUROCYTES OF THE GUT, AND DEAFNESS"],"symbol":"ABCDS","gene_symbols":[],"seed_pmids":[],"max_year":2002},"nodes":[{"id":"entry","type":"Entry","label":"ABCD SYNDROME","mim":"600501","entry_type":"phenotype"},{"id":"section:description","type":"Section","label":"description"},{"id":"section:nomenclature","type":"Section","label":"nomenclature"},{"id":"section:cloning_expression","type":"Section","label":"cloning_expression"},{"id":"section:gene_structure","type":"Section","label":"gene_structure"},{"id":"section:clinical_features","type":"Section","label":"clinical_features"},{"id":"section:other_features","type":"Section","label":"other_features"},{"id":"section:biochemical_features","type":"Section","label":"biochemical_features"},{"id":"section:inheritance","type":"Section","label":"inheritance"},{"id":"section:cytogenetics","type":"Section","label":"cytogenetics"},{"id":"section:mapping","type":"Section","label":"mapping"},{"id":"section:heterogeneity","type":"Section","label":"heterogeneity"},{"id":"section:gene_function","type":"Section","label":"gene_function"},{"id":"section:molecular_genetics","type":"Section","label":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"section:genotype_phenotype_correlations","type":"Section","label":"genotype_phenotype_correlations"},{"id":"section:pathogenesis","type":"Section","label":"pathogenesis"},{"id":"section:diagnosis","type":"Section","label":"diagnosis"},{"id":"section:clinical_management","type":"Section","label":"clinical_management"},{"id":"section:population_genetics","type":"Section","label":"population_genetics"},{"id":"section:evolution","type":"Section","label":"evolution"},{"id":"section:animal_model","type":"Section","label":"animal_model"},{"id":"section:history","type":"Section","label":"history"},{"id":"paper:11891690","type":"Paper","label":"Verheij et al. (2002)","pmid":"11891690","year":2002,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"ABCD syndrome is caused by a homozygous mutation in the EDNRB gene."},{"id":"paper:7778600","type":"Paper","label":"Gross et al. (1995)","pmid":"7778600","year":1995,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Autosomal-recessive neural crest syndrome with albinism, black lock, cell migration disorder of the neurocytes of the gut, and deafness: ABCD syndrome."},{"id":"paper:397773","type":"Paper","label":"Witkop (1979)","pmid":"397773","year":1979,"content_level":"title","relevance":"background","title":"Depigmentations of the general and oral tissues and their genetic foundations."},{"id":"finding:7778600:1","type":"Finding","label":"Gross et al. (1995) reported a macrosomic newborn girl with albinism, a black lock of hair at the right temporo-occipital region, retinal depigmentation, and bilateral deafness confirmed by brainstem auditory-evoked potentials. She also had a severe defect of intestinal innervation: biopsy showed aganglionosis of the large intestine and a total absence of neurocytes and nerve fibers in the small intestine, indicating a total lack of sympathetic and parasympathetic innervation. She died of intestinal dysfunction at 5 weeks of age.","pmid":"7778600","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001520","type":"Phenotype","label":"Large for gestational age","hpo_id":"HP:0001520"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0007513","type":"Phenotype","label":"Generalized hypopigmentation","hpo_id":"HP:0007513"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000953","type":"Phenotype","label":"Hyperpigmentation of the skin","hpo_id":"HP:0000953"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0007894","type":"Phenotype","label":"Fundus hypopigmentation","hpo_id":"HP:0007894"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0008619","type":"Phenotype","label":"Bilateral sensorineural hearing impairment","hpo_id":"HP:0008619"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0002251","type":"Phenotype","label":"Aganglionic megacolon","hpo_id":"HP:0002251"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0004389","type":"Phenotype","label":"Intestinal pseudo-obstruction","hpo_id":"HP:0004389"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001522","type":"Phenotype","label":"Death in infancy","hpo_id":"HP:0001522"},{"id":"inh:AR","type":"Inheritance","label":"Autosomal recessive","hpo_id":"HP:0000007"},{"id":"finding:7778600:2","type":"Finding","label":"Gross et al. (1995) reported that the proband was the 14th child of consanguineous Kurdish parents. Four of her sibs had the same syndrome and died a few days after birth, and the other 9 sibs were well. The authors concluded that the syndrome represents a new neural crest syndrome with autosomal recessive inheritance.","pmid":"7778600","section":"inheritance"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0003811","type":"Phenotype","label":"Neonatal death","hpo_id":"HP:0003811"},{"id":"finding:7778600:3","type":"Finding","label":"Gross et al. (1995) described a syndrome of albinism, black lock, deafness, and a total lack of intestinal neural innervation as a previously unreported neural crest syndrome, and named it ABCD syndrome.","pmid":"7778600","section":"description"},{"id":"finding:11891690:1","type":"Finding","label":"Verheij et al. (2002) described ABCD syndrome as an autosomal recessive syndrome characterized by albinism, black lock, cell migration disorder of the neurocytes of the gut (Hirschsprung disease), and deafness. They noted that the phenotype clearly overlaps with Shah-Waardenburg syndrome, which comprises sensorineural deafness, hypopigmentation of the skin, hair and irides, and Hirschsprung disease.","pmid":"11891690","section":"description"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001022","type":"Phenotype","label":"Albinism","hpo_id":"HP:0001022"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0002211","type":"Phenotype","label":"White forelock","hpo_id":"HP:0002211"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000365","type":"Phenotype","label":"Hearing impairment","hpo_id":"HP:0000365"},{"id":"finding:11891690:2","type":"Finding","label":"Verheij et al. (2002) screened the EDNRB gene in the index patient of the ABCD syndrome family and found a homozygous nonsense mutation in exon 3 (R201X). They suggested that ABCD syndrome is not a separate entity but an expression of Shah-Waardenburg syndrome.","pmid":"11891690","section":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"gene:EDNRB","type":"Gene","label":"EDNRB"},{"id":"variant:EDNRB:p.R201*","type":"Variant","label":"EDNRB p.R201*","gene":"EDNRB","keys":["p.R201*"],"omim_name":"EDNRB, ARG201TER"},{"id":"finding:11891690:3","type":"Finding","label":"Because of the overlap with Shah-Waardenburg syndrome and the finding of a homozygous EDNRB mutation, Verheij et al. (2002) suggested that ABCD syndrome is an expression of Shah-Waardenburg syndrome rather than a separate entity.","pmid":"11891690","section":"heterogeneity"}],"edges":[{"src":"paper:7778600","rel":"reports","dst":"finding:7778600:1"},{"src":"finding:7778600:1","rel":"in_section","dst":"section:clinical_features"},{"src":"finding:7778600:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0001520","pmid":"7778600","present":true,"text":"macrosomia"},{"src":"finding:7778600:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0007513","pmid":"7778600","present":true,"text":"albinism"},{"src":"finding:7778600:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0000953","pmid":"7778600","present":true,"text":"black lock at right temporo-occipital region"},{"src":"finding:7778600:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0007894","pmid":"7778600","present":true,"text":"retinal depigmentation"},{"src":"finding:7778600:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0008619","pmid":"7778600","present":true,"text":"bilateral deafness"},{"src":"finding:7778600:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0002251","pmid":"7778600","present":true,"text":"aganglionosis of the large intestine"},{"src":"finding:7778600:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0004389","pmid":"7778600","present":true,"text":"absence of neurocytes and nerve fibers in the small intestine"},{"src":"finding:7778600:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0001522","pmid":"7778600","present":true,"text":"death in infancy"},{"src":"finding:77